{
  "meta": {
    "product": "Swap",
    "version": "0.9.0",
    "note": "Single source of truth for the switcher's look. `python3 design/gen-tokens.py` writes src/Tokens.swift and windows/Tokens.cs from this file; never edit those by hand. Colours are rgba(r,g,b,a) or `accent@alpha` (the system accent colour at that alpha). Sizes are points on the Mac and device independent pixels at 96 dpi on Windows. Every colour has a dark and a light value: the panel follows the system appearance (or the user's choice in Settings). Optional on a colour: contrastDark and contrastLight replace it when Increase Contrast is on (Mac), and onAccent marks text drawn on the selected row, which Theme turns black on a light accent colour. The `themes` section holds the colour themes: each replaces some of these colours by name, see its note. Stripe sizes: stripeBand is the band along the top edge (the panel grows by stripeBand + stripeBandGap at the top when a theme draws it); the tail on the selected row is stripes stripeTail wide whose tops lean stripeTailSlant to the left, falling like the brand stripes, and rows keep stripeTailReserve clear on the right while a theme has a tail."
  },
